  "scope": "Two bounded groups: actual renderer expansion/truncation projection and ordinary MarkdownPart line-limit caller inputs. No product changes, target execution, build or device operations.",
  "reused_reports": [
    "ios-remote-message-parent-current-20261113-r3.json",
    "ios-remote-user-message-fourth-20261113-findings.json",
    "ios-remote-v476-render-context.json"
  ],
  "observations": [
    {
      "id": "structured-prompt-preparation",
      "type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "sources": [
        "0x95d1c00 ParsedUserMessageMarkdown descriptor",
        "0x1a01688..0x1a017dc",
        "0x1d8e4e8 typepair0x7e122b0",
        "0x1ceec1c",
        "0x2438098"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Renderer input contains optional CodexRenderedItem.ParsedUserMessageMarkdown with _document, _collapsedDocument, markdown and collapsedLineLimit. It copies a supplied prepared projection when available; otherwise 0x2438098 prepares one from source text and the effective collapsedLineLimit.",
      "limits": "The exact cached preparation identity comparison includes input/context and must not be replaced with text-only cache identity. Full parser implementation is not reconstructed."
    },
    {
      "id": "full-versus-collapsed-selection",
      "type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "sources": [
        "0x1a0182c..0x1a0185c",
        "0x1a018d0..0x1a01924",
        "0x1d19de8",
        "0x1ab4f54"
      ],
      "conclusion": "The renderer selects the full document when isExpanded is true or collapsedDocument is absent; otherwise it selects collapsedDocument. Expanded returns expansion-state raw2; unexpanded returns raw1 iff collapsedDocument is present, otherwise raw0. The state and projected rendered blocks are cached together on the renderer.",
      "limits": "These are numeric implementation states observed from the selected consumer, not named official wire enum cases. This does not prove collapse-back interaction or service state."
    },
    {
      "id": "result-to-button",
      "type": "official_artifact_observation-reused-and-corroborated",
      "sources": [
        "0x1a0195c..0x1a01960 return blocks/state",
        "0x1a6bac4..0x1a6bac8 saves returns",
        "0x1a6bb00 passes saved state asx2",
        "0x1a6bb64 keeps lowbyte",
        "0x1a6bdbc..0x1a6bdd4 optional showsExpansionButton override",
        "0x1d19c30..0x1d19c5c Binding setter"
      ],
      "conclusion": "When showsExpansionButton is nil, only renderer-state raw1 admits the expansion sibling. Explicit non-nil bool overrides this admission. The expansion action sets isExpanded Binding true, then rendering selects the full document and the default expansion button goes away. It is not a toggle.",
      "limits": "No explicit expansion-action haptic was found in this scoped direct action. Per-message Binding persistence ownership remains separate."
    },
    {
      "id": "source-line-budget-not-visual-line-budget",
      "type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "sources": [
        "0x2438098..0x24381e0",
        "0x243811c..0x2438148 limit>=1 / limit<sourceLineCount / suffix checks",
        "0x265013c ->0x241d900",
        "0x241d988..0x241d9e8 Unicode scalar newline recognition",
        "0x265dbec ->0x18a2694 source suffix selection"
      ],
      "conclusion": "The effective collapsedLineLimit drives a source-string line projection before Markdown rendering. The line splitter recognizes LF through CR, NEL U+0085 and U+2028/U+2029. A collapsed candidate is omitted when budget is below1, source line count does not exceed it or selected remaining source is absent. This is not a viewport visual wrapped-line count.",
      "limits": "Complete newline-pair/coalescing, trailing-empty and Markdown source slicing reconstruction were not fully proved in this pass. Do not implement a purportedly equivalent splitter merely from the recognized scalar set; use original/prepared projection when available."
    },
    {
      "id": "ordinary-caller-narrowed",
      "type": "official_artifact_observation-plus-bounded-inference",
      "sources": [
        "UserMessageBubble descriptor0x95addb4 field6 heartbeatTrigger",
        "0x1a6cb28 metadata field-vector slot+0x28",
        "0x1a6cb54 constructs address using that offset",
        "0x1a6cb7c Optional single-payload test",
        "typepair0x7e839e0 ->Optional<CodexRemoteHeartbeatTrigger>",
        "0x1a6cbe8 supplies40",
        "0x1a6cc5c supplies2",
        "0x1a6cd04..0x1a6cd10 alternate query selects40/2"
      ],
      "conclusion": "The40/2 input is controlled by owner configuration including heartbeatTrigger Optional admission, not source text length. Metadata independently shows this is CodexRemoteHeartbeatTrigger, whose fields are automationID/currentTimeISO. A second Optional comparison and later0x2421bc8 query also participate; their exact source field/semantic condition was not closed.",
      "limits": "Do not describe40 as the universal user-message default or2 as an ordinary short-message limit. The first nil test alone is insufficient to choose40 globally."
    }
  ],
  "implementable_parent_contract": {
    "classification": "source-backed interface with explicitly independent host renderer adapter",
    "inputs": [
      "stable message id",
      "full source text",
      "optional prepared {document,collapsedDocument,source,collapsedLineLimit}",
      "original markdownOptions",
      "user-input/reference projection and autocompleteItems",
      "linkHandlers and menus",
      "owner-supplied effective collapsedLineLimit",
      "optional showsExpansionButton",
      "per-message expanded Binding"
    ],
    "outputs": [
      "projected prompt blocks",
      "expansion state {noCollapsedCandidate/raw0,collapsedCandidate/raw1,expanded/raw2} local presentation names only"
    ],
    "parent_behavior": [
      "Maintain dedicated prompt renderer separate from assistant Markdown styling.",
      "Compose projected prompt blocks plus conditional expansion sibling in their recovered parent; preserve already-proven bubble geometry.",
      "On expansion set Binding true and re-render full source. No character-count or visual Text measurement guess for original truncation.",
      "When owning fixture does not supply verified line policy, expose an explicit independent fixture policy or omit folding; do not advertise that policy as recovered official default.",
      "Cache by full relevant input/context identity including revision/options/traits/budget/expanded, not solely stable id."
    ],
    "not_ready_for_original_equivalence": [
      "Unclosed effective40/2 caller identity prevents a globally source-equivalent default policy.",
      "Exact source truncation slice/newline semantics, body font/options, inline reference/menu consumers remain partial."
    ]
  },
  "platform_sharing": {
    "iOS_Remote": "actual dedicated CodexRemotePromptMarkdownBlocks consumer proved",
    "iOS_Chat_Work": "No actual shared caller proof in this bounded pass; do not promote this Remote renderer/40/2 policy to Chat or Work.",
    "Android": "not investigated here"
  },
  "precise_unknowns": [
    {
      "boundary": "0x1a6cb40..0x1a6cbdc second Optional comparison and0x2421bc8 input",
      "next_minimum_action": "Bind original metadata/register owner of the second compared optional before assigning a human field name or calling ordinary40 default."
    },
    {
      "boundary": "0x2438098 truncation source slicing through0x18a2694/0x2432c10",
